# Everything excluded from the Docker build context.
#
# The context is the repo root, because shared/ lives there and every service
# imports it. That makes this file load-bearing rather than an optimisation: the
# repo carries a .venv, a node_modules and ~19 MB of tracked vision videos, and
# without pruning them the context is over a gigabyte and every one of those
# layers is invalidated by unrelated edits.
#
# Note what is NOT ignored: data/cache/overpass/. It is copied into the base
# image deliberately (docker/base/Dockerfile) so a fresh `docker compose up`
# answers from seeded data instead of making every container race Overpass for
# the same tiles.

# --- secrets ---
# Never bake credentials into an image layer. Compose passes configuration in as
# environment variables, and every key the services actually read (MOCK,
# DEMO_BBOX, DEMO_RIDER, DEMO_TZ, TRAFFIC_SIDE, S1_URL, S2_URL, S3_URL) is set
# explicitly in docker-compose.yml.
.env
.env.local
secrets.env

# --- vcs and editor state ---
.git
.gitignore
.github
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
*.swp

# --- python ---
# The local venv is 3.14 with a different dependency set than any image, and
# copying it in is how you get a container that runs the host's site-packages
# instead of the ones its own Dockerfile installed.
.venv
venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
*.egg-info
.coverage
htmlcov

# --- logs and transient output ---
logs/
# Local uvicorn logs, not container logs (those go to `docker logs`).
*.log

# --- node ---
frontend/node_modules
# A host build of the same app; the image builds its own from source.
frontend/dist
frontend/.vite
# Vite env files are host-local configuration. The image sets VITE_* through
# build ARGs, and letting a developer's frontend/.env into the build would make
# the image depend on whose machine built it.
frontend/.env
frontend/.env.local
frontend/.env.*.local

# --- data ---
# The Overpass cache is intentionally kept (see header). These two subtrees are
# not: fetched imagery and derived rasters, regenerable and large.
data/cache/images
data/cache/routes
*.tif
*.npy
*.npz

# --- the vision service ---
# services/vision is out of scope for this compose file: it is a batch
# Mask2Former pipeline with no HTTP surface, not one of the four deployed
# processes. Excluded rather than merely unused because it carries ~19 MB of
# tracked MP4s and PNGs, and a 14 MB results/videos/selftest_compare.png.
services/vision
src/

# --- misc ---
# Model weights, wherever they land.
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors
*.onnx
